When `reply` is allocated after locking the ovs_mutex and the allocation fails, it becomes an ERR_PTR. The error handling at `err_unlock_ovs` calls `kfree_skb(reply)`, which expects a valid skb pointer or NULL, not an ERR_PTR, causing a crash.

